slug: timed-up-and-go-gait-speed
title: Timed Up and Go and Gait Speed — Two Minutes That Predict a Lot
area: Skills · Balance & Function
level: Foundation
best: 2nd year onwards
minutes: 12
hook: How long a person takes to stand, walk three metres, turn and sit — and how fast they walk ten metres — says more about falls, hospital stay and survival than many expensive tests. Learn both, correctly. || Insaan ko uthne, teen metre chalne, mur'ne aur baithne mein kitna waqt lagta hai — aur woh das metre kitni tezi se chalta hai — girne, hospital mein qiyam aur zindagi ke baare mein bohat si mehngi tests se zyada batata hai. Dono sahi tareeqay se seekhein.
goal: By the end, you'll perform the Timed Up and Go (TUG) and the 10-metre walk test with the correct set-up, apply the cut-offs and use the clinically meaningful change. || End tak aap sahi setup ke saath Timed Up and Go (TUG) aur 10-metre walk test karenge, cut-offs lagayenge aur clinically ahem tabdeeli use karenge.

say: The **Timed Up and Go (TUG)**: the patient sits back against a chair (usual shoes and walking aid), and on "go" stands, walks **3 metres** at a comfortable and safe pace, turns, walks back and sits; stop the timer when the back touches the chair. **Under 10 s is normal in healthy adults; 12 s or more suggests an increased falls risk (CDC STEADI), and 14 s or more is a stronger warning in community-dwelling older adults.** The **10-metre walk test** measures gait speed: mark a 10 m walkway with 2 m at each end for acceleration and slowing, and time only the **middle 6 metres**. **Gait speed = distance ÷ time.** || **Timed Up and Go (TUG)**: patient chair se peeth laga kar baithta hai (aam jootay aur walking aid), “go” par khara hota hai, **3 metre** aaram aur mehfooz raftar se chalta hai, murta hai, wapas chalta hai aur baithta hai; peeth chair se lagte hi timer rok dein. **Healthy adults mein 10 s se kam normal; 12 s ya zyada girne ka barhta khatra batata hai (CDC STEADI), aur community mein rehne wale buzurgon mein 14 s ya zyada aur bhi sakht warning hai.** **10-metre walk test** gait speed naapta hai: 10 m ka walkway mark karein, dono sirey par 2 m raftar pakarne aur rukne ke liye, aur sirf **beech ke 6 metre** ka waqt lein. **Gait speed = faasla ÷ waqt.**
analogy: Gait speed is the "sixth vital sign". Just as a temperature and a pulse tell you something is wrong without telling you what, a slow walk tells you the person has less reserve across heart, lungs, muscles, brain and balance. TUG is a short obstacle course: it needs strength to rise, balance to turn and control to sit — if any piece is weak, the time lengthens. || Gait speed “chhati vital sign” hai. Jaise temperature aur pulse batate hain ke kuch ghalat hai magar yeh nahi ke kya, aahista chalna batata hai ke insaan ke dil, phephron, muscles, dimagh aur balance mein reserve kam hai. TUG chhota sa obstacle course hai: uthne ke liye taqat, mur'ne ke liye balance aur baithne ke liye control chahiye — koi hissa kamzor ho to waqt lamba ho jata hai.
demo: balance-function/tug :: Timed Up and Go :: Watch the whole route: stand, walk 3 metres to the cone, turn, return and sit. The timer runs from "go" until the back touches the chair; the demo shows a healthy 10.2 s against the 12 s cut-off. The chair, the walkway and the cone are placed as in the real test. || Poora raasta dekhein: khare hon, cone tak 3 metre chalein, murein, wapas aayein aur baithein. Timer “go” se peeth chair se lagne tak chalta hai; demo healthy 10.2 s 12 s cut-off ke muqable mein dikhata hai. Chair, walkway aur cone asli test ki tarah rakhe gaye hain.
check: Which action stops the timer in the TUG? || TUG mein timer kaun si harkat par rukta hai?
ok: When the patient's back touches the chair after sitting down || Jab baithne ke baad patient ki peeth chair se lage || Yes — the whole cycle is stand, walk, turn, return and sit. || Haan — poora cycle khara hona, chalna, murna, wapas aana aur baithna hai.
no: When the patient reaches the cone || Jab patient cone tak pohnche || The turn and return are still part of the test. || Mur'na aur wapsi bhi test ka hissa hain.
no: When the patient stands up || Jab patient khara ho jaye || Standing is only the start. || Khara hona sirf shuruaat hai.
demo: balance-function/ten-mwt :: 10-metre walk test :: The patient walks at a comfortable (or fast) speed; **time only the middle 6 metres** with no coaching during the walk. The demo shows the timer for the middle section and the gait speed that results. Always state whether you tested comfortable or fast speed. || Patient aaram (ya tez) raftar se chalta hai; **sirf beech ke 6 metre** ka waqt lein aur chalte hue koi coaching nahi. Demo beech ke hissay ka timer aur us se banne wali gait speed dikhata hai. Hamesha likhein ke aap ne comfortable ya fast speed test ki.
compare: Interpreting gait speed || Gait speed ka matlab
head: Gait speed || Gait speed ;; Typical meaning || Aam matlab ;; Clinical use || Clinical istemal
row: Below 0.6 m/s || 0.6 m/s se kam ;; Household walker; high risk of falls and hospitalisation || Ghar ke andar chalne wala; girne aur hospital mein dakhil hone ka zyada khatra ;; Intensive rehabilitation, walking aid assessment, home safety || Intensive rehabilitation, walking aid assessment, ghar ki safety
row: 0.6–0.8 m/s || 0.6–0.8 m/s ;; Limited community walking || Mahdood community mein chalna ;; Strength and balance programme; supervised practice outdoors || Taqat aur balance programme; bahar supervised practice
row: 0.8–1.2 m/s || 0.8–1.2 m/s ;; Community walker; crossing a street safely needs about 1.2 m/s || Community mein chalne wala; sarak safely paar karne ke liye takriban 1.2 m/s chahiye ;; Fast-pace practice and dual-task training for street crossing || Sarak paar karne ke liye tez raftar ki practice aur dual-task training
row: 1.2 m/s or more || 1.2 m/s ya zyada ;; Typical of healthy adults || Healthy adults ki aam raftar ;; Maintain; add challenge and variety || Barqarar rakhein; challenge aur variety jorein
mistake: **Changing the test between visits.** Different chairs (seat height 43–46 cm is standard), shoes, walking aids, instructions or speeds make times incomparable. Use the same set-up, read the instructions word for word, do not coach during the walk and note the aid. Do not time from "ready" instead of "go", and do not stop the clock when the patient is still standing. For gait speed, always time only the **middle 6 m**, and state the speed used. || **Visits ke beech test badalna.** Mukhtalif chairs (seat ki unchai 43–46 cm standard hai), jootay, walking aids, instructions ya raftar ka waqt na-qabil-e-muqabla bana deti hain. Wohi setup rakhein, instructions lafz ba lafz parhein, chalte hue coaching na karein aur aid note karein. “Ready” se waqt shuru na karein “go” ke bajaye, aur patient abhi khara ho to ghari rok na dein. Gait speed ke liye hamesha sirf **beech ke 6 m** ka waqt lein, aur istemal ki gayi raftar likhein.
check: A patient needs 14 seconds for the TUG and 0.7 m/s for gait speed. What is the best summary? || Patient ko TUG ke liye 14 seconds aur gait speed 0.7 m/s chahiye. Behtareen khulasa?
ok: Increased falls risk and limited community walking; start strength, balance and walking practice and check the home || Girne ka barha khatra aur mahdood community walking; taqat, balance aur walking practice shuru karein aur ghar check karein || Yes — both measures point the same way; combine them with history and other risk factors. || Haan — dono measures ek hi taraf ishara karte hain; history aur doosre risk factors ke saath milayein.
no: Both are normal for age || Dono umar ke hisaab se normal hain || 14 s and 0.7 m/s are below usual community thresholds. || 14 s aur 0.7 m/s aam community thresholds se neeche hain.
no: The patient is safe to walk unsupervised outdoors || Patient bahar bina nigrani chalne ke liye mehfooz hai || These values suggest limited and risky community ambulation. || Yeh values mahdood aur khatarnak community chalne ki taraf ishara karti hain.
clinic: **Use the numbers to set goals and to show change.** A change of about **0.1 m/s in gait speed** is considered clinically meaningful (small meaningful change about 0.05 m/s) and a TUG improvement of roughly **1–3 seconds** beyond measurement error is real in many groups. Link the numbers to function: "gait speed 0.7 → 0.9 m/s: can now cross a quiet street". Treat the cause (weakness, balance, pain, fear, footwear) rather than only the score. || **Numbers ko goals tay karne aur tabdeeli dikhane ke liye use karein.** Gait speed mein takriban **0.1 m/s** ki tabdeeli clinically ahem maani jati hai (chhoti ahem tabdeeli takriban 0.05 m/s) aur TUG mein measurement error se zyada takriban **1–3 seconds** ki behtari bohat se groups mein asli hai. Numbers ko function se jorein: “gait speed 0.7 → 0.9 m/s: ab khamosh sarak paar kar sakte hain”. Sirf score ke bajaye wajah (kamzori, balance, dard, dar, jootay) ka ilaaj karein.
evidence: A pooled analysis of nearly 35,000 older adults found that **gait speed predicts survival**: each 0.1 m/s faster is associated with a lower risk of death (hazard ratio about 0.88), and speeds around 1.0 m/s corresponded to the median life expectancy for age and sex. TUG alone is a **poor predictor of future falls** in community adults, so use it as one piece of a multifactorial assessment, not as a stand-alone verdict. || Takriban 35,000 buzurgon ka pooled analysis paya ke **gait speed zindagi ka andaza lagati hai**: har 0.1 m/s tez raftar maut ke kam khatray se jori hai (hazard ratio takriban 0.88), aur takriban 1.0 m/s raftar umar aur gender ki median life expectancy ke barabar thi. Akela TUG community adults mein **mustaqbil ki girawat ka kamzor predictor** hai, is liye isay multifactorial assessment ka ek hissa samjhein, akela faisla nahi.
reveal: Why do we time only the middle 6 metres of the 10-metre walkway? || 10-metre walkway ke sirf beech ke 6 metre ka waqt kyun lete hain? || Because the first 2 m are acceleration and the last 2 m are deceleration; timing the steady middle section gives a true walking speed rather than a start-stop speed. It also makes results comparable between clinics. || Kyunke pehle 2 m raftar pakarne aur aakhri 2 m rukne ke hain; steady beech ka hissa naapne se start-stop speed ke bajaye asli chalne ki raftar milti hai. Is se clinics ke beech results comparable bhi hote hain.
check: What gait speed is generally needed to cross a street safely? || Sarak safely paar karne ke liye aam taur par kitni gait speed chahiye?
ok: About 1.2 m/s (traffic-light times are designed around it) || Takriban 1.2 m/s (traffic-light ke waqt isi ke hisaab se banaye jate hain) || Yes — many older adults walk slower than this, so crossing safely needs targeted training. || Haan — bohat se buzurg isse aahista chalte hain, is liye safely paar karne ke liye targeted training chahiye.
no: About 0.4 m/s || Takriban 0.4 m/s || That is far too slow for most crossings. || Zyada tar crossings ke liye yeh bohat aahista hai.
no: About 2.0 m/s || Takriban 2.0 m/s || That is a fast jogging-pace walk, not needed. || Yeh tez jogging jaisi raftar hai, zaroori nahi.
safety: **Guard the patient.** Stand close on the weaker side with a gait belt for the TUG, especially with balance problems; stop if the patient becomes unsteady, dizzy, breathless or in pain. Check orthostatic blood pressure and recent falls first. Refer unexplained falls, blackouts (syncope), new neurological signs or sudden functional decline for medical review before testing again. || **Patient ki hifazat karein.** TUG ke liye kamzor side par gait belt ke saath qareeb khare hon, khaas taur par balance ki takleef mein; patient unsteady, chakkar, saans ki takleef ya dard mein ho to ruk jayein. Pehle orthostatic blood pressure aur haali girawat check karein. Be-wajah girawat, blackouts (syncope), nayi neurological signs ya achanak functional girawat ko dobara test karne se pehle medical review ke liye refer karein.
summary: TUG: stand, walk 3 m, turn, return, sit; 12 s or more suggests a falls risk (CDC STEADI), 14 s or more is a stronger warning. || TUG: khare hon, 3 m chalein, murein, wapas aayein, baithein; 12 s ya zyada girne ka khatra (CDC STEADI), 14 s ya zyada sakht warning.
summary: Gait speed = distance ÷ time over the middle 6 m of a 10 m walkway; 1.2 m/s is needed to cross a street and 0.1 m/s is meaningful change. || Gait speed = 10 m walkway ke beech ke 6 m par faasla ÷ waqt; sarak paar karne ke liye 1.2 m/s chahiye aur 0.1 m/s ahem tabdeeli hai.
summary: Standardise the set-up, never change the test between visits and combine the numbers with history, since TUG alone does not predict falls well. || Setup standardise karein, visits ke beech test na badlein aur numbers ko history ke saath milayein, kyunke akela TUG girna acchi tarah predict nahi karta.
card: TUG cut-offs for falls risk? || TUG ke girne ke khatray ke cut-offs? || 12 s or more (CDC STEADI); 14 s or more is a stronger warning in older adults. || 12 s ya zyada (CDC STEADI); buzurgon mein 14 s ya zyada sakht warning.
card: How is gait speed measured? || Gait speed kaise naapi jati hai? || 10 m walkway, time only the middle 6 m; speed = distance ÷ time. || 10 m walkway, sirf beech ke 6 m ka waqt; speed = faasla ÷ waqt.
card: Clinically meaningful change in gait speed? || Gait speed mein clinically ahem tabdeeli? || About 0.1 m/s (small meaningful change about 0.05 m/s). || Takriban 0.1 m/s (chhoti ahem tabdeeli takriban 0.05 m/s).
card: Gait speed needed to cross a street safely? || Sarak safely paar karne ke liye gait speed? || About 1.2 m/s. || Takriban 1.2 m/s.
